  "note": "forward gaps reflect the live bf16 lm_head of the NF4-loaded verifier vs this bf16->f32 lm_head on the float16-logged h; the inverse is the identity logits = W_U h_a with W_U of full column rank, solved by float64 normal equations (rel_err from float32 logits is the float32 rounding floor; f64_logits_* shows the identity itself); top-k recovery uses the RECOMPUTED logits' top-k (id, log-prob) pairs, SVD least squares over [h, logZ] with no ridge (minimum-norm when k < d + 1); r2_* are per-row R^2 about the row's own mean in raw h space, NOT Stage-R's standardized pooled-MSE R^2; bf16 rounding is round-to-nearest-even emulated on float32"
